# Jira

Jira runs through the `jira` MCP server. Never write raw `curl` against the Jira API.

## Approval

Every write is drafted for the user before it is sent. Show the exact comment text,
worklog or field change and wait for a yes. Reads need no approval.

## Which tool

Dedicated tools first: `jira_get_issue`, `jira_ls_issues`, `jira_ls_comments`,
`jira_add_comment`, `jira_create_issue`, `jira_ls_projects`, `jira_ls_statuses`.

Everything else goes through the generic REST verbs `jira_get`, `jira_post`, `jira_put`,
`jira_patch`, `jira_delete`:

```
worklogs      GET|POST   /rest/api/2/issue/{key}/worklog
              PUT|DELETE /rest/api/2/issue/{key}/worklog/{id}
transitions   GET|POST   /rest/api/3/issue/{key}/transitions
edit fields   PUT        /rest/api/3/issue/{key}
assignee      PUT        /rest/api/3/issue/{key}/assignee
edit comment  PUT        /rest/api/2/issue/{key}/comment/{id}
```

## The v2 rule

When your request body contains text you wrote, use `/rest/api/2/`. Otherwise use
`/rest/api/3/`. Version 3 demands Atlassian Document Format, a deep JSON tree. Version 2
takes the same field as a plain string and converts it server side.

```json
POST /rest/api/2/issue/AR-664/worklog
{ "timeSpent": "2h30m", "started": "2026-09-09T09:00:00.000+0530",
  "comment": "Traced the forced sign-out to the session cookie clear." }
```

`started` is strict: `YYYY-MM-DDTHH:mm:ss.SSS±hhmm`. Milliseconds required, no colon in
the offset. `timeSpent` uses Jira units: `2h`, `45m`, `1h30m`, `1d`.

## Rules

- Resolve the issue key from the git branch when the user does not give one.
  `fix/ar-664-accept-invite` means `AR-664`. Two repos: `areasim-backend`, `areasim-webapp`.
- Read before writing. List comments or worklogs first so you edit an existing entry
  rather than adding a near-duplicate.
- Never guess a status name. Fetch transitions and post the transition id.
- Record what you wrote in `docs/jira/<KEY>.md` under today's date, including the id the
  API returned.
- Never invent progress. If you cannot substantiate a claim from the diff, the journal or
  the user, leave it out.
- Project key `AR`.
